ated canadians who have been gone  less than 72 hours so that's good for  those who want to do some cross-border  shopping or see a sporting event or a  concert in the u.s but the entry  requirement is expected to remain for  all foreign nationals including  americans and for canadians out of the  country longer than three days the  question that the the government will  have to answer is  how are you safe  in the 72nd hour and you become  dangerous in the 73rd  what is the logic of this the prime  minister of canada trudeau wouldn't say  much about the new border rules we are  looking at  making making steps to  to loosen up requirements while at the  same time keeping canadians safe but he  did talk privately about them with  congressional leaders like nancy pelosi  and kevin mccarthy chuck schumer and  mitch mcconnell  other border management issues and  rising u.s protectionism were also on  the agenda on thursday the leaders will  get down to business and they'd say  they'll be looking to craft a north  american strategy to deal with covet in  the economy to deal with climate change  and to deal with chyna donna okay david  aiken in washington dc thanks  queen elizabeth back to her royal duties  that's coming up  [Music]  one of the most recognizable riders from  the january sixth attack on the u.s  capitol has been sentenced to 41 months  in prison jacob chansley stormed the  building wearing a horned hat and face  paint he was among the first riders to  disrupt lawmakers meeting to certify  president joe biden's election he  pleaded guilty to obstructing an  official proceeding he is among 650  people charged after the riot  queen elizabeth is back on her feet  today she carried out her first  in-person engagement in a month  she met with the head of britain's armed  forces who is due to step down at the  end of november one of the queen's  beloved dogs was there too the 95 year  old had been following doctor's orders  to rest since spending a night in the  h